    "background_story": "Daisy was a mountain beaver living in the rugged wilderness of the Pacific Northwest. She was a proud member of the aplodontia family, known for their remarkable ability to dig complex burrows. Daisy's home was a marvel of engineering, with tunnels and chambers that protected her from harsh weather and predators. Her aplodontia heritage gave her a unique set of teeth, perfect for gnawing on tough plant material and shaping the wooden structures of her burrow. As she went about her day, gathering branches and aquatic plants for her meals, Daisy took great pride in her work. She was a testament to the ingenuity and adaptability of her species, thriving in the challenging environment of the mountainous terrain.",
